A||||3||Wolfhound||Throttle cable fix||||1
Z||000000||Wolfhound||11-04-1999||06:29 AM||||Just noticed the mention of a burned throttle cable in the mall. A while back I had the cable get against the manifold in a 85 four cylinder on the interstate. By the time I stopped I had almost zero throttle. The cable housing had melted.<BR> After it cooled enough to handle I stretched it back in place and managed to find a stick and bridge the melted housing. I used  duct tape to secure the ends of the stick to each side of the housing. This got me home where I could deal with it proper.<BR>Thought this info might save someone a tow!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Shiner||11-04-1999||01:05 PM||||When I melted mine, I used a piece of duct tape to, and safety wire (the kind you twist, great stuff) to keep the part where it melted straight, so that it didn't have to rely on the plastic housing.  It gave me about half throttle, enough to get home.  I pulled a throttle cable from an '85, only to find out that it is different!  Let me tell you, this is NOT the most fun thing in the world to do, and if you are not limber, have the shop do it.  You have to be able to contort your body into all kinds of comprimising positions to get at the damn thing, heh.||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroGT||11-04-1999||04:58 PM||||Shiner:<P>Been there, done that, got the greasy t-shirt to prove it. Let me guess, you have an '84, right? The only thing different about that cable is the end clip that attaches to the throttle body, if I'm not mistaken. You could have used the cable from the '85 if you grabbed the bracket, as well. Pain in the @$$ to put in, but beats the $45 or so the dealer wanted for the cable.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Shiner||11-04-1999||11:27 PM||||FieroGT,<P> Yep, it was my '84 SC that smoked that cable.  It's the stupidest place to put the thing; right over the manifold.  I will never buy another '84 again (unless it's a mint Indy, with 4.11 gears! hehe)  I am much more happy with my GT.  It's still a pain in the ass, but with that kind of performance, its worth while, and then some!||||reg||10
